cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or reference Mapping Voices in research, teaching, or another
  project, please cite it as below.
title: "Mapping Voices: An Atlas of Oral-History and Voice-Testimony Archives"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Abubakar
    given-names: Adamu
repository-code: "https://github.com/adab-tech/mapping"
url: "https://adab-tech.github.io/mapping/"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - oral history
  - voice testimony
  - archives
  - cultural heritage
  - open data
abstract: >-
  Mapping Voices is an open, interactive atlas of real, publicly documented
  oral-history and voice-testimony archive collections worldwide, filterable
  by country, theme, language, and decade. Each entry links directly to its
  holding institution's own public page. The application source code is
  MIT-licensed; the underlying dataset (data/collections.json) is licensed
  under CC BY 4.0 — see LICENSE for the split and its rationale.
